    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
      {
        "@value": "CONS_IVR description clarified to the voids ratio at the start of the increment rather than repeat the initial voids ratio on each record in the CONS group as listed in previous editions.\nCONS_TEMP - BS1377 and BS EN ISO 17892-5 requires laboratory temperature at which test was carried out, but since Cv is corrected to 20 DegC from the temperature over the stage, it has to be per stage (but may be same throughout).\nBS allows reporting of either CONS_CVRT or CONS_CVLG or both, the laboratory will populate these headings as appropriate.",
